.TH AIO-CLI 1 "August 2026" "aio 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aio-cli \- aio command line interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aio
.RB [ \-\-cli ]
.RI [ action ]
.RI [ argument ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The CLI is the default interface. With no arguments it prints the numbered
catalogue of all available public pygame games:
.PP
.B "aio" \fR→ prints "Built-in / PyPI / GitHub / Awesome" sections and the total.
.PP
Every game is identified by a continuous number (built-in 1-39, PyPI
40-386, GitHub 387-549, awesome 550-561) as well as a name; both work for
launch and install.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.BR list " / " games " / " help
Print the catalogue.
.TP
.BR launch " " name-or-number
Launch a game. Examples:
.br
.B aio launch aliens
.RS
built-in pygame example
.RE
.br
.B aio launch 163
.RS
launch by number (PyPI package)
.RE
.br
.B aio launch https://github.com/user/repo.git
.RS
clone-and-run a repository
.RE
.TP
.BR install " " target
Install a game by name or number, a git repository, or a requirements file.
Examples:
.br
.B aio install 550
.RS
install pyscroll (awesome list) via pip
.RE
.br
.B aio install -r requirements.txt
.RS
install a requirements file
.RE
.TP
.BR doctor
Print component availability (curses, tkinter, pystray, jinja2, cython).
.TP
.BR build " " system " " [ args ]
Build integration:
.IR cython " file.py" ,
.IR cmake " source_dir build_dir" ,
.IR ninja " build_dir" ,
.IR meson " build_dir source_dir" ,
.IR cargo " [target]" .
.TP
.BR jinja " " ...
Jinja2 templating helpers.
.TP
.BR docs " " format
Regenerate documentation:
.IR markdown ", " html ", " man ", " doxygen ", " all .
.TP
.BR hello " [" name ]
Echo demo.
.SH LAUNCH / INSTALL SEMANTICS
Built-in examples run with
.BR "python -m pygame.examples.<name>" .
PyPI packages are installed on demand and run with
.BR "python -m <pkg>" .
GitHub and awesome entries are cloned into a temporary directory; if a
runnable entry point exists it is executed, otherwise the repository is
reported as a library and
.B install
is suggested.
.PP
Missing modules are auto-installed (pyopengl, numpy, pillow,
opencv-python, ...) and the launch retried once.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on operational errors (unknown action, missing argument,
failed launch or install), 130 when interrupted.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aio (1),
.BR aio-tui (1),
.BR aio-suite (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Jimmy + opencode
